  ],
  "texto": "You've been manipulated. By a partner. A friend. Even your own family. And it was never an accident. It has a name — 5 of them. Therapists see these same 5 patterns in almost every unhealthy relationship — romantic, family, even at work. Learn just ONE, and they lose their power over you. Forever. Number one: gaslighting. They make you doubt your own memory. Your own eyes. 'That never happened.' 'You're overreacting.' 'You're crazy.' It's not confusion. It's control. And it works — because you start believing them. Number two: love bombing. Too much, too fast. Gifts, texts, 'soulmate' — in week one. It's not passion. It's a hook. The faster it starts, the harder it can trap you. Real love doesn't need to rush. Number three: the silent treatment. Not space. A punishment. They go cold on purpose — until you apologize for THEIR mistake. Silence, weaponized. If this happened to you — like this video right now. Number four: guilt-tripping. 'After everything I've done for you...' Turning your needs into your fault. If you feel guilty for having limits — that's the tactic working. Guilt is not love. It's leverage. Number five: moving the goalposts. You finally do what they asked. Suddenly, it's not enough. The target keeps moving — so you can never win. That's the point. You're not supposed to win. There is no version of you that would ever be enough for them. Once you can name it... ...it loses its power over you. This isn't love. It's a playbook. And now you've read it. Comment the NUMBER that hit hardest. Send this to someone stuck in one of these. And follow for the next 5 — because there's more.",
